{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TraceConventionGate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TraceConventionGate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.traceConvention_factor_determined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.traceConvention_factor_determined","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TraceConventionGate.lean#L79-L85","doc":"**I-6 (uniqueness / no hidden DOF).** Once the canonical convention is\nfixed (`trFbor ≠ 0`), the relating factor is uniquely determined\n`c = trChiCache / trFbor` — the convention freedom is not a free parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.traceConventions_distinct_of_factor_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.traceConventions_distinct_of_factor_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TraceConventionGate.lean#L68-L77","doc":"**I-6 (distinctness).** If the chi-cache trace relates to the F_Bor braid\ntrace by `trChiCache = c · trFbor` with `trFbor > 0` and `c ≠ 1`, the two\nconventions give genuinely different numbers. (Compute: `c = R_p ≈ 1.0668`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.no_uniform_scalar_density","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.no_uniform_scalar_density","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TraceConventionGate.lean#L43-L66","doc":"**I-1 — no uniform scalar per-knot density.**\nIf the proton/neutron chi-cache traces are ≥ 1.15 asymmetric\n(`trp ≥ (115/100)·trn`) while the round-trip densities are ≤ 1.001\nnear-degenerate (`rp ≤ (1001/1000)·rn`), then there is NO knot-independent\nscalar `f` with `ρ = f · tr_M` for both nucleons. Scope-(b) exclusion of the\nuniform-scalar density family (the cited invariant is this impossibility). ","signatureChunk":0}]}